WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:19.798
The sun had been shining on the secret garden for nearly a week.

2
00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:25.678
Mary was beginning to like being outdoors, and she was even starting to like the wind.

3
00:00:25.679 --> 00:00:30.541
She could run faster and longer, and she could skip up to a hundred.

4
00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:38.168
Mary was a determined little person, and now that she had something to be interested in, she was very determined.

5
00:00:38.169 --> 00:00:42.492
She worked hard in the garden, digging and pulling up weeds.

6
00:00:42.493 --> 00:00:46.125
Instead of getting tired, she felt happy.

7
00:00:46.126 --> 00:00:52.237
During that week of sunshine, Mary met Ben Weatherstaff outdoors several times.

8
00:00:52.238 --> 00:00:59.578
She always approached quietly because she was afraid he might pick up his tools and leave if he saw her.

9
00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:06.066
"You are like the robin," he said to her one morning when she suddenly appeared at his side.

10
00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.661
"I never know when I will see you."

11
00:01:08.662 --> 00:01:12.452
"The robin is friends with me now," said Mary.

12
00:01:12.453 --> 00:01:16.480
Ben stopped working and rested one foot on his shovel.

13
00:01:16.481 --> 00:01:19.025
"How long have you lived here?"

14
00:01:19.026 --> 00:01:21.606
"I think it's been about a month."

15
00:01:21.607 --> 00:01:23.665
"You're starting to look better.

16
00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:27.525
Your face is not so pale, and you look fatter."

17
00:01:27.526 --> 00:01:32.451
"I know I'm fatter," said Mary. "My stockings are getting tighter.

18
00:01:32.452 --> 00:01:35.080
Oh, look, there's the robin!"

19
00:01:35.081 --> 00:01:38.847
The robin hopped closer and closer to Ben.

20
00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:44.372
He spread his wings, flew up in the air, and landed on the handle of Ben's shovel.

21
00:01:44.373 --> 00:01:47.743
Ben looked as if he didn't dare to breathe.

22
00:01:47.744 --> 00:01:51.645
Then the robin flew away, and Ben took a breath.

23
00:01:51.646 --> 00:01:56.069
There was a smile on his face as he went back to digging.

24
00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.348
Ben's smile gave Mary the courage to ask a question.

25
00:02:00.349 --> 00:02:03.361
"Do you have a garden of your own?"

26
00:02:03.362 --> 00:02:05.537
Ben shook his head.

27
00:02:05.538 --> 00:02:09.768
"But if you did, what kind of flowers would you plant?"

28
00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:16.583
"Bulbs, but mostly roses. I was a gardener for a young lady who loved roses.

29
00:02:16.584 --> 00:02:20.110
She had a lot in a place she was fond of.

30
00:02:20.111 --> 00:02:23.167
I even saw her bend over and kiss them."

31
00:02:23.168 --> 00:02:28.763
He pulled out a weed and frowned at it. "But that was ten years ago."

32
00:02:28.764 --> 00:02:31.106
"Where is she now?"

33
00:02:31.107 --> 00:02:32.634
"Heaven."

34
00:02:32.635 --> 00:02:38.402
"And what happened to her roses?" asked Mary. "Did they die too?"

35
00:02:38.403 --> 00:02:43.994
"Once or twice a year, I'd go and work at them. I'd prune them and dig around their roots.

36
00:02:43.995 --> 00:02:48.249
But I haven't gone this year. I'm too old to do all that work."

37
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.570
Mary couldn't stop asking questions.

38
00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:56.997
"When the roses have no leaves, how can you tell if they're dead or alive?"

39
00:02:56.998 --> 00:03:00.586
"Look for little brown lumps swelling along the branches.

40
00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:04.671
Then watch them after a warm spring rain and see what happens."

41
00:03:04.672 --> 00:03:10.195
Ben suddenly looked angry. "Why do you care so much about roses?

42
00:03:10.196 --> 00:03:14.503
Go away and play. I'm done talking for today."

43
00:03:14.504 --> 00:03:20.796
Mary skipped down the garden path. She liked Ben even when he was gruff.

44
00:03:20.797 --> 00:03:24.082
Suddenly she stopped skipping.

45
00:03:24.083 --> 00:03:28.705
A red-haired boy sat under a tree, playing a wooden pipe.

46
00:03:28.706 --> 00:03:31.343
But he wasn't the only one there.

47
00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:36.433
A brown squirrel was clinging to the trunk of the tree and watching him.

48
00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:41.267
A pheasant was peeping out from behind a bush.

49
00:03:41.268 --> 00:03:44.981
Two brown rabbits were inching closer to the boy.

50
00:03:44.982 --> 00:03:49.739
All the animals seemed to be listening intently to the music.

51
00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:55.687
"Shh," the boy said to Mary. "Stay quiet or you'll frighten them away."

52
00:03:55.688 --> 00:03:58.813
He finished playing and stood up slowly.

53
00:03:58.814 --> 00:04:04.228
The bird and the animals wandered away, but they didn't seem afraid.

54
00:04:04.229 --> 00:04:09.117
"I'm Dickon," said the boy. "And you must be Miss Mary.

55
00:04:09.118 --> 00:04:11.854
I have your seeds and your tools."

56
00:04:11.855 --> 00:04:15.042
He pointed to a brown package on the ground.

57
00:04:15.043 --> 00:04:19.303
"Let's sit down on this log and look at them," said Mary.

58
00:04:19.304 --> 00:04:22.440
Dickon unwrapped the package.

59
00:04:22.441 --> 00:04:27.785
He showed her a shovel, a rake, a hoe, a fork, and a trowel.

60
00:04:27.786 --> 00:04:32.570
There were also two packets of seeds for blue and white flowers.

61
00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:36.262
"I'll plant these for you myself. Where's your garden?"

62
00:04:36.263 --> 00:04:42.055
Mary didn't know what to say. Could she trust this strange boy?

63
00:04:42.056 --> 00:04:46.354
"Can you keep a secret?" she blurted out at last.

64
00:04:46.355 --> 00:04:51.144
Dickon looked puzzled. "I keep secrets from the other boys all the time.

65
00:04:51.145 --> 00:04:57.281
If I couldn't keep secrets about fox cubs and bird nests, nothing would be safe on the moor."

66
00:04:57.282 --> 00:05:03.480
Mary grabbed his sleeve. "I've stolen a garden," she said quickly.

67
00:05:03.481 --> 00:05:06.659
"Nobody wants it. Nobody cares for it.

68
00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:13.082
Nobody ever goes into it. Maybe everything is dead in it; I don't know.

69
00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:17.756
But they can't take it away from me when I care about it and nobody else does."

70
00:05:17.757 --> 00:05:20.724
And then she burst into tears.

71
00:05:20.725 --> 00:05:26.731
Dickon's eyes grew wide. "Where is this garden?" he said softly.

72
00:05:26.732 --> 00:05:37.089
Mary got up from the log. "Come with me, and I'll show you."
